AB  - Investigated and compared the incidence and development of restlessness, bedwetting, thumb sucking, nail biting, temper tantrums, sleep walking, food fads, and sexual misconduct in 180 mentally retarded (aged 6–20 yrs, IQ < 70) Ss from socially advantaged and disadvantaged Indian families. It was found that all 8 behaviors developed, with restlessness and temper tantrums occurring most frequently. Disadvantaged Ss displayed significantly greater restlessness, temper tantrums, and food fads. Bed wetting and thumb sucking were found to occur more often among the socially advantaged group. It is concluded that neurotic traits are effective indicators of social factors. (11 ref) (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
