AB  - Explores the effects of cognitive group interventions on 76 depressed frail elderly nursing home residents. First, we briefly review cognitive-behavioral and focused visual imagery therapies for depressed older adults and the extent to which prior research offers insight and direction regarding the use of these interventions with depressed nursing home residents. We report on research that evaluates the effects of these treatments for depressed nursing home residents. Specifically, using the factor structure of the Geriatric Depression Scale (GDS), we reanalyzed our data to examine whether the original findings on the outcome of depression manifest themselves across the 6 dimensions of the GDS, or whether differentiated effects on selective dimensions of depression in late life can be identified. Similarly, using the factor structure of the Modified Mini-Mental State Examination, we reanalyzed the data to look at differential effects across major dimensions of neurocognitive function. Results showed that either therapy, conducted over a 24-wk period, reduces depressive symptomatology in this population. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2020 APA, all rights reserved)
