AB  - Outlines strategies for chemical dependency intervention with Vietnam veterans. The intake interview ascertains length of service, type of discharge, when the client arrived in Vietnam, feelings about Vietnam, and assigned location. Clinicians should assess posttraumatic stress disorder (PTSD) symptoms, such as nightmares, flashbacks, or hypervigilance. Once the PTSD symptoms are identified, the client must cease the use of chemicals/alcohol, and this may require hospitalization. Clients must be reassured that although PTSD symptoms may return, they will learn to control them in therapy sessions. Veterans and their families should be referred for group therapy in conjunction with substance abuse therapy. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2019 APA, all rights reserved)
