AB  - INTERVENTION: Arm 1: Group‐based yoga exercise program. Participants allocated to the group‐based yoga exercise program will be offered attendance at yoga classes in trial‐specific groups of 15‐25 people at established yoga studios with experienced yoga teachers. Participants will aim to attend 80, one‐hour duration classes in total on a twice‐weekly basis, over the 12‐month period. Participants will be also asked to complete a home‐based yoga program for at least two 20‐minute sessions each week. The yoga classes will be provided free of charge to participants. Class content will emphasise standing yoga postures that challenge balance and build leg strength. The program will be tailored to participant ability and progression of difficulty for each posture will occur as skills and confidence increase. The program is based on the Iyengar style of yoga which was chosen as it involves holding static postures rather than flowing movements, which is likely to be simpler to learn and has been used successfully with older adults. Iyengar yoga also uses aids (â€œpropsâ€? e.g. blocks, straps) to modify the postures and to enable people with a range of functional abilities to participate, making it the ideal style for older people. Intervention adherence will be recorded by yoga teachers who will keep class attendance records and participants who will keep home yoga practise diaries. CONDITION: Falls ; ; Falls; Injuries and Accidents ‐ Other injuries and accidents PRIMARY OUTCOME: Number of falls in the 12 months after randomisation, assessed using monthly falls calendars.[12 month period after randomisation.] SECONDARY OUTCOME: Balance self‐confidence assessed with the Activity‐specific Balance Confidence Scale‐ Simplified[Baseline and 12 months after randomisation] Cost‐effectiveness of delivering the intervention, fall‐related and total costs of health and community service utilisation. Health‐system and community‐service contact will be collected on a monthly basis along with the falls calendars. Participants will be asked to mark on the monthly postal questionnaire each time they use a health and community service (e.g. GP, physiotherapist, nurse).[12‐month period after randomisation.] Goal attainment measured with the Goal Attainment Scale.[12 months after randomisation ] Mental wellbeing assessed using the Warwick‐Edinburgh Mental Well‐being Scale.[Baseline and 12 months after randomisation] Pain assessed with specific study developed questions [Baseline and 12 months after randomisation] Physical function assessed with the lower limb function subscale of the Late Life Function and Disability Instrument.[Baseline and 12 months after randomisation] Process evaluation using semi‐structured interviews with yoga instructors and participants.[12 and 18 months after randomisation.] Quality of life assessed using the EQ‐5D‐5L.[Baseline and 12 months after randomisation] Self‐reported overall physical activity, planned activity and home exercise assessed with the Incidental and Planned Exercise Questionnaire.[Baseline and 12 months after randomisation] Sleep quality and disturbances measured using Pittsburg Sleep Quality Index.[Baseline and 12 months after randomisation ] INCLUSION CRITERIA: Eligible participants will: a) Be aged 60 years and over; b) Live independently at home; c) Not currently participate in yoga; d) Be able to travel to an intervention location.
