AB  - INTERVENTION: Treatment Arm: Weekly 60 minute group movement‐based yoga and mindfulness classes for 12 weeks (~5‐6 participants per class). The program will teach mindfulness meditation through breathing and a set of postures that are appropriate for a beginner. The classes will allow for progression, but participants are always able to adjust to the level that best suits them on the day. Intervention will be delivered by trained and experienced yoga teachers (one lead and one assistant per class). Adherence will be monitored using attendance logs. 20 minutes home practice of mindfulness meditation daily (provided on CD/audio link). Adherence will be monitored using participant diary. CONDITION: Stroke ‐ Haemorrhagic Stroke ‐ Ischaemic Stroke; ; Stroke PRIMARY OUTCOME: Composite primary: Changes in brain structure (i.e. cortical thickness and resting state connectivity) assessed using Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI) brain scans[Baseline, and at 12 weeks after intervention commencement (~13 weeks) ] SECONDARY OUTCOME: Blood cholesterol assessed by CardioChek+ Portable Lipids Test Kit[Baseline, and at 12 weeks after intervention commencement (~13 weeks) ] Blood glucose (HbA1c) assessed by A1CNow+ Portable HbA1c Test Kit[Baseline, and at 12 weeks after intervention commencement (~13 weeks) ] Blood pressure assessed by OMRON blood pressure monitor[Baseline, and at 12 weeks after intervention commencement (~13 weeks) ] Cognitive function assessed by Trail Making Test‐B Test (executive attention); and n‐back task for working memory[Baseline, and at 12 weeks after intervention commencement (~13 weeks)] Fatigue assessed using the Fatigue Assessment Scale [Baseline, and at 12 weeks after intervention commencement (~13 weeks) ] General feedback will be assessed using qualitative interviews. These interviews will be group face‐to‐face sessions, and include open‐ended questions. The interviews will be audio‐recorded, and will run for around 60 minutes. [12 weeks after intervention commencement (~13 weeks)] Health status and Quality of life assessed using the SIS and EQ‐5D‐3L questionnaires. ; [Baseline, and at 12 weeks after intervention commencement (~13 weeks) ] Mood assessed using Hospital Anxiety and Depression Scale and the Depression Anxiety Stress Scale[Baseline, and at 12 weeks after intervention commencement (~13 weeks) ] Satisfaction with program will be assessed using study specific questionnaires for the intervention and control group with a combination of questions seeking responses on a 5 point Likert scale and open ended questions[12 weeks after intervention commencement (~13 weeks)] Stress assessed by cortisol levels in hair ; [Baseline, and at 12 weeks after intervention commencement (~13 weeks) ; ] INCLUSION CRITERIA: â€¢ Aged 18 years or more â€¢ Confirmed diagnosis of stroke whereby the last stroke event is between 3 and 12 months â€¢ Participants living in the community (not nursing home or aged care residential facilities) within 30 kms of BrainPark (770 Blackburn Rd, Clayton VIC 3168, Australia) â€¢ Have access to email and/or SMS (to access home practice guide, and receive class reminders) â€¢ Self‐identify as users of electronic technology such as CD player (to access home practice guide) â€¢ Have a baseline Modified Rankin Score of 0 (i.e. no disability) to 4 (i.e. may require some assistance but not constant care); â€¢ Able to give informed written consent and can understand two‐step verbal commands; already enrolled in other clinical trial, as long as there will be no issues with contamination to either trial, and that there is assurance that responder burden is minimal
