AB  - Developed the STIDD, a series of 15 multiple-choice vignettes that pose clinical dilemmas in the pharmacotherapy of patients with psychoactive substance use disorders coexisting with other mental disorders. 14 psychiatrists served as judges and standardized the treatment options along a treatment integration continuum. 69 male and 42 female psychiatrists were surveyed with the vignettes and 3 subscales of the Substance Abuse Attitude Survey, described by J. N. Chappel et al (see record [rid]1986-00121-001[/rid]). 10 of the 15 vignettes were taken to form the normally distributed STIDD, which is described in terms of its reliability and validity. Females selected treatment approaches that addressed the substance use disorder to a greater extent than those selected by males. Sample vignettes and treatment options are appended. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2019 APA, all rights reserved)
