AB  - 43 Native American alcoholics (mean age 31.8 yrs), 20 Native American nonalcoholics (mean age 33.5 yrs), 20 Anglo alcoholics (mean age 35.9 yrs), and 17 Anglo nonalcoholics were compared on demographics and on the Rokeach Value Survey. Alcoholic Ss were from an inpatient alcohol treatment program of a rural community mental health center. Results confirm the poorer prognostic rates of alcoholism recovery for Native American alcoholics. Data also suggest that Native Americans' values are measurable and significantly different from Anglo values. Anglos assigned significantly higher values to societal goals, while the Native Americans preferred more personal and group-oriented values. It is suggested that the disparity in values between the 2 cultures is one reason why so few Native American alcoholics remain in treatment. (24 ref) (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2019 APA, all rights reserved)
