AB  - Describes the authors' experiences in establishing and conducting concurrent support groups for homeless mothers and their preschool children. The purpose of the parents' group was to promote discussion of grief, other emotionally distressing topics, coping strategies, and parenting skills in a supportive climate. The foci of the preschoolers' group were to enhance social skills, increase awareness of personal hygiene and health, and stimulate the learning of basic developmental skills. Goals for the joint activities were to promote positive parent–child interaction, increase parent awareness of child developmental capabilities and limitations, and provide role modeling of healthy interactions. An incentive program used to promote attendance in the parent's group is described. Recommendations for successful intervention with homeless families are provided. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
