AB  - A broad, interdisciplinary approach is needed to solve the mysteries of functional mental retardation. A study framework is proposed which relates the individual's life process to the social systems that affect it. Such a framework has advantages for epidemiology, formulation of research hypotheses, and optimizing use of scarce intervention resources. It also recognizes that mental illness or other social problems also may be caused by the same dysfunctioning social systems, and encourages joint efforts toward common results.
