AB  - Following the integration in July 1989 of family planning services into 13 drug treatment programs in Philadelphia, Pa, baseline interviews were conducted with 599 female participants. Findings show that 75% had a sexually transmitted disease, & even though they were in a drug treatment program, 41% had injected drugs in the previous month, & 62% had engaged in sexual activity without using a contraceptive. Twelve months into the program, 7 focus groups were conducted with 65 women & men to learn more about their opinions & attitudes related to contraceptives & family planning services in general. The discussions revealed that many participants were still unsure what family planning services included, saw no need for such services, or did not want them because of prior negative experiences with health care providers. There was also considerable misinformation about contraceptives & their effects on health. 2 Tables. Adapted from the source document.
