AB  - Mental health issues and emotional distress are a common occurrence in multiple sclerosis (MS), and are often under diagnosed and under treated; resulting in reduced functioning, increased disability and reduced quality of life. Research has suggested that treatments such as antidepressants and cognitive behaviour therapy are effective in alleviating mental health issues in MS, although it appears that many people with MS have difficulty accessing the appropriate mental health care. This paper outlines an initiative to improve access to mental health care and treatment for people with MS. It highlights the importance of joint working across boundaries for improved patient care and suggests management strategies for people experiencing mental distress in the context of multiple sclerosis.
