AB  - Reviews the history of community-based treatment for offenders with drug and alcohol addiction. The authors describe the treatment regimen in 2 residential programs for offenders (aged 20-50+ yrs) with drug and alcohol problems--1 that treats state offenders, and 1 that treats county offenders. The authors include a description of the components of the residential treatment model utilized in these 2 programs that employs a progressive Level System, group and individual therapy, as well as educational and employment interventions that support community reintegration. Findings support the efficacy of coerced drug and alcohol residential treatment for forensic clients that receive state or county sentences. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2019 APA, all rights reserved)
