AB  - The article investigates the effectiveness of integrated motivational interviewing and cognitive behavioral therapy (CBT) for the treatment of patients with psychosis and a co-morbid substance misuse problem. It reports that over a follow-up period of 24 months, no difference in the rate of relapse of psychotic symptoms could be found between the control and treatment groups. However, the integrated motivational interviewing and CBT-based intervention did reduce the amount of substance consumed by a majority of the patients on a using day.
