AB  - Evaluated is a pilot demonstration program providing residential treatment for clients dually diagnosed with severe mental illness & substance use disorders in NH. Three phases of treatment are described: (1) preadmission evaluation, program admission, & the first 3-4 weeks of treatment; (2) the attainment of abstinence & residents' active participation in substance-oriented group treatment; & (3) client involvement in the process of discharge planning & making the transition back into the community. The challenges & difficulties of each phase of treatment are discussed, & several modifications in the program are recommended with regard to engagement in treatment, community integration, length of treatment, & treatment philosophy. 9 References. Adapted from the source document.
