AB  - The article reports that group psychotherapy helped reduce post-traumatic stress disorder (PTSD) among survivors of sexual violence in the Democratic Republic of Congo, a low-income, conflict-affected country. It also highlights the reduction in combined depression and anxiety symptoms and improvement in functioning among the survivors. The results of the treatments are also discussed including individual support and cognitive processing therapy.
