AB  - Based on the author's experience with long-term groups of severely affected alcohol and drug dependents, it is argued that alcoholics and drug dependents need, for constant crisis management, a long-term group. Since they become group dependent, they cannot be without the group; otherwise they would relapse into their alcohol or drug dependence. Their group dependence is not a negative effect, since it helps the participants to remain free of alcohol and drugs and to work through their emotional and cognitive crises with the co-members. As far as the alcohol dependents are concerned, it should also be considered that, because of their brain damage, they are often not able to introject the group for a long time, and therefore they have to see and to feel the group over and over again if they are to remain abstinent. Group discussions with the spouses may help to consolidate the results attained within the group of patients. (French & German abstracts) (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
