AB  - This article focuses on legislation related to mental health treatment in prisons. Passed with bipartisan sponsorship and support in the U.S. Senate in October 2003. The House version of the bill is currently in committee in the House of Representatives. It would parcel out funds as seed grants, with matching state funds increasing over time, to joint applicants from criminal justice and mental health organizations. Initiatives eligible for funding include mental health courts that incorporate treatment components into sentencing, training programs for mental health and criminal justice personnel so improve recognition and responsiveness to mental illness in offenders, and programs that facilitate transition from incarceration to community and increase access to community based mental health care.
