AB  - An on-site community support system team in a single room occupancy hotel worked with 36 homeless mentally ill women toward rehabilitation through empowerment. The issue of power in the group process over a 5-yr period is described and analyzed. A focus on group members' strengths is intended to counteract the effects of alienation, hopelessness, and despair that developed from life on the streets and within psychiatric institutions. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2020 APA, all rights reserved)
