AB  - The article presents an overview of the study that evaluates the effects of a 90-day day-care program for chronic psychotic patients from lower socioeconomic backgrounds. The program uses a goal attainment approach, and offered socialization, support and group therapy. The results of the study shows no significant changes in self-report measures of the degree and type of psychopathology, or in attitude toward mental illness and treatment. Changes represented by attainment of goals were obtained, but the goals were simplistic that they hardly represents a significant behavior change.
