AB  - A substantial and growing percentage of older adults misuse alcohol, prescription drugs, or other substances. Older adults with alcohol problems are a special and vulnerable population that can benefit from elder-specific relapse prevention strategies focused on the unique issues associated with alcohol abuse and medication misuse in later life. Topics discussed in this chapter include prevalence and impact of substance abuse among older adults; projected demographic trends; lifetime patterns of drinking; identifying substance use problems in older adults; interventions and treatments for older adults; treatment outcomes; current research on relapse; relapse prevention; group treatment approach; treatment modules; brief interventions; and co-occurring disorders including depression, Alzheimer's disease, alcohol-associated cognitive impairment, and sleep disorders. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2020 APA, all rights reserved)
