AB  - This study examined participation in 12-step programs and attitudes toward 12-step meetings in an outpatient sample of 81 severely mentally ill patients with comorbid substance use disorders. The study found that dual diagnosis patients attended 12-step programs at rates comparable to those reported for patients in primary addiction treatment sellings. Diagnosis and attitudes toward 12-step meetings each had independent effects on 12-step participation. The difficulties that some dual diagnosis patients report experiencing at 12-step meetings may need to be addressed to maximize 12-step attendance and potential to benefit from 12-step programs.
