AB  - Examined the psychiatric comorbidity in 24 hospitalized women (aged 17–35 yrs) with bulimia. Ss completed the Eating Attitude Test, Eating Disorders Inventory, Hawkins Binge Scale, and Beck Depression Inventory at both admission and discharge. The standardized treatment program included behavioral techniques, structured group treatment, and individual treatment using cognitive restructuring, psychodynamically oriented procedures, and supportive psychotherapy. More than 50% of Ss had 2 or 3 Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders-III-Revised (DSM-III-R) axis I disorders in addition to bulimia nervosa, and almost 50% of Ss met criteria for at least 1 personality disorder. Findings suggest an added negative impact of anxiety disorder on the improvement of bulimic behavior and possibly on self-rated depression. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2020 APA, all rights reserved)
