AB  - Presents the case of a 27-yr-old married father with a history of obsessive sexual thoughts about children since the age of 7 yrs. He was arrested for exposing his genitalia to a group of children and attempting to seduce them. At referral, he was diagnosed with pedophilia and dysthymic disorder and begun on standard antipsychotic treatment. He reported freedom from the obsessive sexual thoughts while on a trial of risperidone and fluoxetine combined. His depressed mood and low self-esteem also showed improvement, and he was able to plan for outpatient group therapy. The possibility that paraphilias may represent an obsessive-compulsive spectrum disorder is discussed. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
