AB  - The plenary session consisted of four papers presented by Professors Jess Huerta De Soto, Angelo Santagostino, Francesco Forte, and Dr. Gordon L. Brady. Professor De Soto's paper is entitled, An Austrian Defense of the Euro and the Current Anti-deflationist Paranoia. Professor Santagostino's paper is entitled, Einaudi, EU Competencies, Fiscal Policy, and the Missing Maastricht. Professor Francesco Fortes jointly-authored paper is titled, On the Long-Run Negative Effects of Public Deficit on Unemployment and the Need for a Fiscal Constitution: An Empirical Study of OECD Countries. Dr. Gordon L. Bradys paper is entitled, Austerity in the European Union: Keynesian Stimulus Versus Fiscal Consolidation.
