AB  - The article reports that the Brandeis/Harvard Center on Managed Care and Drug Abuse Treatment plans to work on three research projects as well as a pilot initiative involving parity legislation and substance abuse treatment. The center's research will include the following: Substance Abuse Treatment Pathways for Employee Groups; Profiling and Incentives in Behavioral Health Care; Substance Abuse Treatment and Work; The Effect of Parity Legislation on Substance Abuse Treatment. The specific aims of this pilot research are to examine the impact of parity for substance abuse treatment on the in-network cost of health care, substance abuse care and mental health care.
