AB  - Discussed is the utility of several measures for evaluating the temporal effects of social interventions: log-linear modeling, structural equation modeling, repeated measures analysis of variance, & time-series analysis. The methods are demonstrated using secondary data on the independent & joint effects of methadone maintenance & legal supervision on narcotics use & property crime among 4 groups of heroin addicts (total N = 1,688) in Calif. The multimethod assessment demonstrates that methadone maintenance has both short- & long-term suppressive effects on narcotic use & property crime; complementary findings are revealed for the effects of legal supervision. 1 Table, 4 Figures, 41 References. Adapted from the source document.
