AB  - Study was made to learn the extent of drug abuse coming to the attention of treatment personnel in private and public facilities within one urban community during a 1-month period. Reports from 105 facilities indicated alcohol was the major drug of abuse with heroin and nonopiate drugs running a distant second and third, respectively. Of 8,784 requests for treatment in which the use of drugs was seen as a factor, 83% involved alcohol, 9% opiates, 6% nonopiate, nonalcoholic drugs, and 2% unknown drugs.
