AB  - 36 father–daughter/stepdaughter sexual abusers, classified as regressed according to A. N. Groth's (1978) typology, were followed over a 2-yr outpatient treatment program. Degree of personality disturbance as assessed by the Minnesota Multiphasic Personality Inventory (MMPI), stress level, and substance abuse potential were recorded before beginning treatment. 23 Ss completed the program. Completing Ss were rated on progress at posttreatment in terms of emotional congruence, sexual arousal, blockage, internal inhibitors, acceptance of responsibility, and empathy with the victim. The more personality-disturbed Ss showed lower rates of program completion and attainment of empathy for the victim. Criminal prosecution was related to improved empathy and trends toward slightly higher progress ratings. Careful pretreatment personality assessment is stressed. (French & Spanish abstracts) (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2020 APA, all rights reserved)
