AB  - A comparison of the lifestyles & personality traits of 145 drinking patients & 148 obese clients attending outpatient programs in Newport Beach, Calif, & with matched control groups (N = 114 + 98, respectively). Data obtained via various checklists, inventions, & scales indicate that both treatment groups manifest dissatisfaction with all aspects of their lives: obese clients have lower self-confidence & orientation toward achievement, & feel more passive & alienated than do problem drinkers. Problem drinkers experience a greater variety of problems & treat them more unconventionally than do obese clients. Both groups manifest characteristics of impulsivity, dependency, & self-abasement. 4 Tables, 22 References. A. Devic
