AB  - A shortened form of the Parental Bonding Instrument (PBI) and the Hospital Anxiety and Depression Scale were administered to 122 male offenders (aged 15–22 yrs) held in custody in Scotland. High levels of psychological distress were linked with low parental care, but there were no associations between psychological distress and parental control. However, an analysis of the factor structure found that, although the care factor of the PBI showed good internal reliability, the control factor was less well defined in this group. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2019 APA, all rights reserved)
