AB  - Objective: To study the effect of rheumatoid arthritis (RA) on patients' work disability and analyze the factors that contribute to work disability. Method(s): Data were obtained from outpatient and inpatient with RA, randomly selected from Department of Rheumatology in The First Affiliated Hospital of Baotou Medical College, obtain patients' consent, the questionnaire were completed by the rheumatologist, Records of patients with general information and working condition, disease complications, include data about their age, disease duration, employment status, retired because of illness or illness reduce workload, both joint deformity, bone osteoporosis, depression, pathological fracture, interstitial lung disease were collected. The effective questionnaires were 256 cases. A nonparameter test and multivariate Logistic regression analysis were performed. Demographic data was shown by descriptive analysis. Student'S t-test was used for categorical data analysis. Chi-square and Logistic regression analysis were used to assess the power of RA related indexes as predictors of work disability. Result(s): Totally 256 completed data were collected. The ratio of male to female was 1:4.2. The mean age were (52 +/- 14.2) years. The ratio of patients who retired before the average age were 30.3%, 20% had to cut-down the load of work, Only 20.2%of the patients remained their work status. Data analysis showed that low income (c2 = 15.462,P < 0.05), low education level (c2 = 18.39,P < 0.05) and high HAQ (c2 = 7.859,P < 0.05) effected on patients' work ability. Conclusion(s): RA have a profound effect on patients' work ability in China, especially in patients with low education level, low income, and high HAQ score.
