AB  - Placed 64 nursing home patients receiving doxepin, other psychoactive drugs, or no medication on an alcohol regimen of beer or wine in the ward or in a simulated pub setup. The alcohol produced significant improvement in all groups, especially the doxepin group. However, the pub milieu did not demonstrate a significant superiority over ward milieu. It is suggested that the pub milieu should be used as a catalyzer rather than as an independent treatment modality to facilitate the alcohol therapy. (18 ref.) (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
