AB  - Currently, there is no basis to grant passes in detention to persons against whom the preventive measure referred to in Art. 94 of the Criminal Code is applied. The position of the Supreme Court (decision of 28 September 2006, Ref. I KZP 23/06) allowing the opportunity to grant a pass to a detained person under the rules of organization and order of the establishment is incorrect. This leads to the determination of the status of detainees in instruments which were not a source of universally binding law (Art. 87 of the Constitution). Regulation of the Minister of the Health of 10 August 2004 on the list of psychiatric and drug treatment facilities designed to carry out preventive measures - forming the grounds for the normative position of the SC - determines only the rules of organization and order of establishments with maximum and enhanced security conditions, ordering the use of the internal rules of the given establishment with respect to the detainees to whom basic preventive measures are applied. Thus it transfers the power of the minister to determine the rules onto directors of psychiatric institutions, which may lead to the use of norms and practices incompatible with the Act on the Protection of Mental Health, preventing the detainees from being granted passes (Art. 37).
