AB  - Cost-effectiveness studies require the estimation of overall program effectiveness using multiple outcome measures. However, the relative importance of the different outcomes must first be established, a process often accomplished using the Delphi technique. Using an iterative process of group discussion, voting, & feedback of results, 15 Veterans Administration & Community Health Center administrators & clinicians ranked 9 outcome scales in priority, & assigned importance weights. Improvement in client ability to be self-supporting was judged the most important treatment outcome, with symptom reduction second. Involvement with friends & substance abuse were judged the least important outcomes. The groups achieved a high degree of consensus, as measured by convergence toward increasingly precise & distinct importance weights. 4 Tables, 1 Figure. Modified HA.
