AB  - Suggests that providing consultation to staff in a group format is particularly relevant for alcoholism treatment facilities. The complexities involved in alcohol dependency and the life time recovery process for clients make it likely that staff members will experience common practice dilemmas that can be more easily addressed in a group format. Principles of effectiveness to maximize staff learning from group consultation are delineated. These include the following: (1) Explore the staff's values and experiences with alcohol on their practice; (2) demonstrate group work skills and rehearse applications; (3) acknowledge common job frustrations and practice dilemmas related to clients' problems with alcohol that can be barriers to the application of learning; and (4) involve administrators in group consultation to actively assist staff in resolving those barriers. Alcohol treatment groups in one mental health center are discussed. (0 ref) (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2020 APA, all rights reserved)
