AB  - To examine the perception of neighbors regarding the effects of group homes on their neighborhoods, 513 neighbors & 126 nonneighbors of 29 group homes in Charlotte, NC, were interviewed. For both negative (eg, noise, traffic) & positive effects (eg, learning about disabilities), nonneighbors expected that group homes would have a much greater impact than was actually reported by neighbors. These results support prior findings that expectations of negative effects are much greater than actual experiences. 2 Tables, 13 References. Adapted from the source document.
