AB  - INTERVENTION: Intervention1: Effectiveness of a Healthcare Governance Model: A cross sectional study will be done in the Phase I of the research study which includes collection of data using interviewer administered questionnaire among tribal population in the community, Focus Group Discussion and In‐Depth Interview among the healthcare provides catering to the tribal population. Based on the analysis of findings in Phase I, a Healthcare Governance Model will be developed and implemented among the experimental arm, along with other routine health care services offered by PHC. In the controlled arm, additional interventions will not be offered other than the regular routine health care activities offered by PHC. At the end of the course of implementation of Health care Governance Model, the outcome will be assessed in terms of enhanced utilization of health care services from PHC, by the tribal population in the study area. The outcome will be assessed in three follow up visits in the interval of three, six and 12 months period. Control Intervention1: Effectiveness of a Healthcare Governance Model: A cross sectional study will be done in the Phase I of the research study which includes collection of data using interviewer administered questionnaire among tribal population in the community, Focus Group Discussion and In‐Depth Interview among the healthcare provides catering to the tribal population. Based on the analysis of findings in Phase I, a Healthcare Governance Model will be developed and implemented among the experimental arm, along with other routine health care services offered by PHC. In the controlled arm, additional interventions will not be offered other than the regular routine health care activities offered by PHC. At the end of the course of implementation of Health care Governance Model, the outcome will be assessed in terms of enhanced utilization of health care services from PHC, by the tribal population in the study area. The outcome will be assessed in three CONDITION: Healthy Human Volunteers Who Belong to Tribal Community of Udupi District, Who do not Possess Any form of Deformities or Communicable Diseases. PRIMARY OUTCOME: Enhancement in the utilization of health care services offered by PHC, by having an improvement in the health care utilization in the areas of Communicable diseases, reproductive health and mental healthTimepoint: At base line, 3 months, 6 months and 12 months SECONDARY OUTCOME: Implementation of the Healthcare Governance Model through PHC, ; Sustainability of the implementation of Healthcare Governance Model to have a better healthcare outcomeTimepoint: 1 year ; 2 year ; 3 year INCLUSION CRITERIA: Those who are responsive and able to give information by communicating. Members who are consenting to participate in the study
