AB  - INTERVENTION: Intervention1: Metacognitive Training for Depression: The main aim of the training program is to help patients understand cognitive biases and their role in the disorder. This is done through exercises and activities in the therapy modules. Patients are guided in an informal and non confrontational manner to realize how biased thinking maintains the disorder. The therapeutic type of intervention is intended as a supportive care therapy, to be used adjunct with the psychopharmacological treatment for depression. The program is non confrontational and is conducted in a group format where patient participation is encouraged but it is not mandatory. Each module is translated into the local language and is conducted via a power point presentation in an auditorium with ten patients in one session. The program consists of eight modules which addresses different cognitive biases and maladaptive strategies used by patients along with helpful strategies that can be practiced. Each module is conducted for one hour. The participants will be given homework assignments and exercise cards after the first session. Each session begins with revising the previous modules and addressing any concerns. Each session ends with group discussions. Control Intervention1: Treatment as Usual: The active control group will be receiving the psychoeducation module after their pre intervention assessment is completed. The module will include the following: Symptoms of depression Signs to keep in mind to seek immediate help Importance of maintaining a structured routine everyday Importance of physical exercises, examples of simple exercises Relaxation Techniques and steps Information about support groups for patients with depression Contact numbers of suicide helplines CONDITION: Health Condition 1: F33‐ Major depressive disorder, recurrent PRIMARY OUTCOME: Hamilton Depression Rating Scale (HAM‐D)Timepoint: Before the start of the intervention ; Once the intervention is completed ; Six months after the intervention is completed SECONDARY OUTCOME: Brief Coping Orientation to Problems Experienced Inventory. ; Timepoint: Before the start of the intervention ; Once the intervention is completed ; Six months after the intervention is completed ; Cognitive Distortions Scale (CDS)Timepoint: Before the start of the intervention ; Once the intervention is completed ; Six months after the intervention is completed ; Dysfunctional Attitude Scale short form A (DAS‐SF1)Timepoint: Before the start of the intervention ; Once the intervention is completed ; Six months after the intervention is completed ; Metacognitions Questionnaire (MCQ)Timepoint: Before the start of the intervention ; Once the intervention is completed ; Six months after the intervention is completed ; Ruminative Response Scale (RRS)Timepoint: Before the start of the intervention ; Once the intervention is completed ; Six months after the intervention is completed ; Social and Occupational Functioning ScaleTimepoint: Before the start of the intervention ; Once the intervention is completed ; Six months after the intervention is completed ; INCLUSION CRITERIA: 1.Diagnosis of single episode of major depressive disorder without psychotic symptoms 2.Diagnosis of recurrent episodes of major depressive disorder without psychotic symptoms 3.Ability to read and write Tamil
