AB  - Data from various measures were used to examine program perceptions of 367 probationers admitted in 1995 to a 4-month residential drug abuse treatment facility (in Mansfield, TX) that focuses on group counseling. Prior research has shown that many individuals in the criminal justice system have both psychological & drug abuse problems, & often have limited success in drug abuse treatment programs. Focus here is on whether the benefits of node-link mapping, a visual representation counseling technique that is especially beneficial in group counseling environments, would extend to individuals with psychological problems. Probationers were randomly assigned to mapping-enhanced or standard counseling. Those who had greater psychological problems, & who received mapping-enhanced counseling, had more favorable perceptions of their counselors & fellow community members over time than their counterparts who received standard counseling. 2 Tables, 2 Figures, 41 References. Adapted from the source document.
