AB  - Institutional theory is used to develop predictions about organizational units that moved from an environment making consistent demands to one making conflicting demands. Many community mental health centers have diversified into drug abuse treatment. The units providing such services face conflicting demands from the traditional mental health sector and the new drug abuse treatment sector concerning which clients to serve, how to assess their problems, and who should provide treatment. It is proposed that, in response to such demands, the units will adopt apparently conflicting practices. In addition, isomorphism with the traditional sector will be positively associated with external support from the parent mental health centers. The data were drawn from a US study of drug abuse treatment units. The results generally support these predictions.
