AB  - The use of support groups as a clinical intervention for families of the mentally-impaired elderly is suggested in a discussion of senile dementia, & how it impacts on family caretakers. Research on the role of the middle-aged family member as the main source of support for the older adult has suggested that feelings of burden are especially related to the availability of social support (eg, Zarit, S., Reever, K., & Bach-Peterson, J., "Relatives of the Impaired Elderly: Correlates of Feelings of Burden," The Gerontologist, 1980, 20, 6). The role of the social worker in the implementation of family support groups is considered. 13 References. Modified HA.
