AB  - The article discusses U.S. youth in long-term recovery. According to the authors, there is a national preoccupation with the negative aspects of drugs and youth. They argue that U.S. national youth drug policy and funding has been limited to criminalization strategies, prevention programs that provide limited evidence to support their effectiveness, and messages exhorting youth to not use drugs and refrain from drinking until the age of 21. They discuss the increasing number of youths in long-term substance abuse recovery programs and offer a call for the redirection of U.S. national policy and resources to underwrite more funding for adolescent addiction treatment and recovery programs is presented.
