AB  - Focus is on the implementation & outcome of a grief group study conducted with 20 substance abusers, who were chosen through a stratified random sampling from a residential drug & alcohol treatment facility. Ss were divided into experimental & control groups to test the efficacy of the group therapy. Data were obtained by (1) scores on the Beck Depression Inventory, (2) evaluation of pre- & posttest good-bye letters written by Ss to the lost loved one, & (3) a self-administered questionnaire. Results indicate that treatment group participants were significantly less depressed & better able to resolve painful feelings about their losses. The grief group approach is generic & can be modified to meet the needs of varied target groups. The distinctive approach & the empirical results both were completed by a clinician without disrupting the facility, patients, or clinician's daily practices. 1 Table, 19 References. Modified HA
