AB  - In assessing the socioenvironmental characteristics of psychiatric treatment programs, researchers typically assume that their measurements are unaffected by client characteristics, However, the authors' analysis among mentally ill chemical abusers in a therapeutic community and community residences found significant associations between subscales of the Community Oriented Program Evaluation Scale (COPES) and depressive symptoms, as measured by the CES-D, after 2, 6, and 12 months of treatment. Investigators of treatment environments should consider depressive symptoms as a possible threat to the validity of their findings. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2020 APA, all rights reserved)
