AB  - The article focuses on the efforts of the Central Wyoming Counseling Center in reducing costs of the state budget of Wyoming. The Center, led by David Monhollen, conducted a residential treatment program to aid drug addicts and people with mental disorders by outpatient treatments them instead of depending on hospital care, which costs 700 to 1,000 dollars per day. The services, which worth about 87 dollars each, drove the Wyoming state government not to cut funding on the program.
